00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:42.060
play anymore scp-3663 only feels comfortable in&nbsp;
tunnels and will teleport away in distress if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:42.060 --> 00:34:47.100
confined anywhere else as such its containment&nbsp;
chamber is technically the maintenance tunnels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:47.100 --> 00:34:53.100
underneath site 54 Where it seems to have made&nbsp;
a home for itself occasionally if it experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:53.100 --> 00:34:58.680
fear damage or stress it may de-manifest and&nbsp;
appear in tunnels elsewhere at that point the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:05.460
box cutters are deployed to collect 36 60 E3 once&nbsp;
again and bring him back to site 54. so far there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:11.880
has only been one major Containment Breach with&nbsp;
scp-3663 but it was a little more deadly than you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:16.980
might expect for a boy-sized creature made of&nbsp;
cardboard the tunnel monster escaped from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:16.980 --> 00:35:23.280
site-54 tunnels and began wailing in pain it went&nbsp;
positively berserk attacking surrounding staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:28.200
and trashing parts of the facility anyone who&nbsp;
heard the whales of the tunnel monster reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:28.200 --> 00:35:33.840
becoming extremely psychologically disturbed by&nbsp;
them during this four hour Rampage the monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:40.320
also tried multiple times to destroy itself with&nbsp;
various implements but was unsuccessful after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:40.320 --> 00:35:47.460
scp-3663 was recontained two deceased members of&nbsp;
personnel were recovered from the scene autopsies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:47.460 --> 00:35:51.720
showed the cause of death was a buildup of&nbsp;
paper residue and wood pulp in all of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:51.720 --> 00:35:58.140
major blood vessels as well as sinuses ear tubes&nbsp;
and the majority of the digestive and respiratory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:58.140 --> 00:36:03.420
systems a number of other staff members were found&nbsp;
to have been affected to a lesser degree but are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:03.420 --> 00:36:09.720
expected to make full recoveries what triggered&nbsp;
this explosive and deadly Outburst not even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:09.720 --> 00:36:16.680
tunnel monster itself knew the answer to this&nbsp;
question but we do at exactly the same time a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:16.680 --> 00:36:22.860
79 year old man passed away from natural causes&nbsp;
after what seemed like a thoroughly unremarkable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:22.860 --> 00:36:29.760
life that man's name was Johnny a man is sitting&nbsp;
in a chair inside a containment cell at the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:34.800
Foundation the man is dressed normally and he&nbsp;
isn't trying to escape or attack the researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:40.020
who are observing him the only thing that makes&nbsp;
this man different from you or I is that he ages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:40.020 --> 00:36:47.160
right in front of us going from a teenager to an&nbsp;
old man in a matter of minutes at first glance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:47.160 --> 00:36:55.140
scp-1007 looks very normal just a corpse lying in&nbsp;
a standard coffin well the corpse of an old man in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:55.140 --> 00:36:59.700
a coffin being kept locked up in a containment&nbsp;
chamber is normal when compared to some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:04.920
other strange anomalies that that are found&nbsp;
in the SCP foundation's archives inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:04.920 --> 00:37:11.820
coffin with scp-1007 is a small Metal Key and&nbsp;
this is quite literally the key to seeing what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:11.820 --> 00:37:19.020
makes this anomaly so special on scp-1007's back&nbsp;
between his shoulder blades is a small Keyhole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:19.020 --> 00:37:25.440
x-ray scans of 1007 have shown that the keyhole is&nbsp;
just an empty socket it's unconnected to anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:30.960
there's no internal Clockwork mechanisms or other&nbsp;
Machinery that should be able to be activated by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:30.960 --> 00:37:39.780
key when the metal key that is kept in scp-1007's&nbsp;
coffin classified as scp-1007-1 is inserted into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:39.780 --> 00:37:46.740
the keyhole on 1007's back in turn something&nbsp;
truly incredible happens as the key is turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:46.740 --> 00:37:55.020
scp-1007 undergoes a change unlike anything the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation has seen before with each turn of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:55.020 --> 00:38:01.320
the key the subject's physical age is reversed by&nbsp;
one full year Foundation researchers are able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:01.320 --> 00:38:08.340
watch 1007 age in Reverse in real time even any&nbsp;
Decay that had set in on the corpse is completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:08.340 --> 00:38:15.000
reversed and disappears as the key is wound in one&nbsp;
zero zero seven gets younger and younger as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:21.720
key is turned 1007 will continue to DH physically&nbsp;
compacting and shrinking down until it appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:27.540
to have the form of a newborn human child it's&nbsp;
unknown where the physical mass of 1007's body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:27.540 --> 00:38:33.420
goes to since this should defy the laws of physics&nbsp;
but those laws we assume to be a Bedrock of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:33.420 --> 00:38:39.180
universe's reality are often more of a suggestion&nbsp;
when it comes to anomalies the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:39.180 --> 00:38:46.740
deals with Once scp-1007 reaches the newborn baby&nbsp;
stage it will suddenly reactivate coming to life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:46.740 --> 00:38:52.800
immediately regardless of how long it has been&nbsp;
dead and lying in its coffin once 1007 is brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:52.800 --> 00:38:59.340
back to life he will go through the entire human&nbsp;
life cycle within a 75 minute period experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:04.740
what looks to be approximately one year of normal&nbsp;
human growth and development for every minute that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:04.740 --> 00:39:11.580
passes that means that in the course of about&nbsp;
16 minutes researchers will see scp-1007 change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:11.580 --> 00:39:17.280
from a crying infant to a fully grown teenager as&nbsp;
you can imagine the subject has reported feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:17.280 --> 00:39:23.580
excruciating pain during these first few minutes&nbsp;
as his bones rapidly lengthen and expand and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:23.580 --> 00:39:29.880
muscles develop and change shape dramatically&nbsp;
scp-1007 is able to watch with his young eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:29.880 --> 00:39:35.640
as his bones move and set themselves into place&nbsp;
lengthening and widening in seconds during growth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:35.640 --> 00:39:41.040
spurts that normally take months or years after&nbsp;
about five minutes provided his legs have grown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:47.520
to the same length at the same time he's usually&nbsp;
able to prop himself up and stand at around 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:47.520 --> 00:39:53.640
minutes the pain really starts the bones crack&nbsp;
and ache as they grow at their fastest for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:53.640 --> 00:39:59.220
whole cycle hair will also grow on his face and&nbsp;
body and he can't help but feel some amount of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:59.220 --> 00:40:03.840
Shame and embarrassment at what's happening to&nbsp;
him in front of the foundation researchers who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:03.840 --> 00:40:10.260
are taking copious notes by 20 minutes he can&nbsp;
hardly think due to the pain at this point he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:10.260 --> 00:40:15.840
usually lies down and curls into a ball whispering&nbsp;
to himself that it will all be over soon that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:15.840 --> 00:40:21.660
pain won't last forever after another 10 minutes&nbsp;
he's right the pain is almost stopped completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:21.660 --> 00:40:26.880
by the 30-minute mark But now as wrinkles and&nbsp;
stretch marks start to set in a different kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:26.880 --> 00:40:34.980
of pain reveals itself as scp-1007 realizes that&nbsp;
he must watch himself die 40 minutes in and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:34.980 --> 00:40:41.040
starts to reflect on his past the life he was&nbsp;
forced to lead as a kind of Sideshow freak more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:47.040
on that later though the physical Decay happens&nbsp;
faster now warts and moles and other marks of age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:47.040 --> 00:40:53.280
appearing on his skin after 50 minutes he is aware&nbsp;
that over half of his life has passed and he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:53.280 --> 00:40:58.980
reaching the end his hair starts to fall out as do&nbsp;
his teeth which he's never actually been able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:58.980 --> 00:41:05.760
use as he's never tasted food as the 60-minute&nbsp;
mark comes and goes he begins to feel grateful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:11.700
for the coming end with the escape from Pain and&nbsp;
the rest it would bring his body has become very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:11.700 --> 00:41:16.860
wrinkled by this point and is covered with age&nbsp;
spots his eyes begin to Cloud severely limiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:16.860 --> 00:41:21.780
his ability to see and his hearing gets weaker&nbsp;
and weaker until he can't comprehend anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:21.780 --> 00:41:30.540
the researchers say at 75 minutes it's all over&nbsp;
scp-1007's body expires and he dies once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:31.260 --> 00:41:36.660
he will remain as a corpse until the metal key&nbsp;
is inserted into his back and the whole process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:43.260
starts once again just as there appears to be&nbsp;
no explanation for where the mass of scp-1007's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:49.320
body goes as the key is wound during the reversal&nbsp;
process so too is there no explanation for where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:49.320 --> 00:41:54.300
the energy needed for his rapid growth comes&nbsp;
from this process should violate the first law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:54.300 --> 00:42:00.840
of thermodynamics and Foundation researchers are&nbsp;
very curious about the underlying process the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:07.200
constant that remains on scp-1007's body is a&nbsp;
small tattoo on his right calf where the words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:07.200 --> 00:42:14.640
Mr life and Mr death from Little misters by Dr&nbsp;
wondertainment appear this matches up with entry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:22.740
number 11 on document scp-909 which lists&nbsp;
a total of 20 little misters scp-1007 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:22.740 --> 00:42:28.320
recovered by task force Tau 6 during a raid on&nbsp;
a mansion in California along with several other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:35.280
anomalous creatures and objects the owner of the&nbsp;
Mansion claimed that he acquired scp-1007 at an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:42.060
auction hosted by Marshall Carter and dark Limited&nbsp;
Marshall Carter and dark limited is a club based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:42.060 --> 00:42:46.920
in London England that is famed for collecting&nbsp;
and selling what it would describe as rare and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:46.920 --> 00:42:52.980
obscure objects unfortunately this often includes&nbsp;
various anomalies that should be under the care of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:52.980 --> 00:42:58.800
the SCP Foundation and the club's mission to&nbsp;
provide its members with exclusive expensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:04.140
and rare experiences means that they're often in&nbsp;
conflict with the foundation and they have even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:04.140 --> 00:43:10.080
been responsible for several containment breaches&nbsp;
Marshall Carter and dark limited continues to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:10.080 --> 00:43:15.240
a very secretive organization and the name of&nbsp;
the director and a list of its members have so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:15.240 --> 00:43:21.660
far been very difficult to obtain at the auction&nbsp;
they hosted where scp-1007 was offered for sale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:21.660 --> 00:43:27.600
there were apparently along with Mr life and&nbsp;
death at least four other misters for sale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:32.880
though the identity of the other buyers and which&nbsp;
little misters they may have purchased is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:32.880 --> 00:43:41.280
under investigation the fact that scp-1007 has the&nbsp;
name Mr life and Mr death seems to imply that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:41.280 --> 00:43:46.380
may have originally been part of a set though this&nbsp;
counterpart little Mister has yet to be recovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:46.380 --> 00:43:53.700
or even identified in interviews with scp-1007 he&nbsp;
has given his own personal theory that he embodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:53.700 --> 00:43:58.620
both names and the designation is a reference&nbsp;
to the way he alternates between life and death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:59.160 --> 00:44:05.040
however the possibility Still Remains though that&nbsp;
he may have a twin of sorts and the foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:12.720
continues to investigate its possible identity&nbsp;
and location scp-1007's brief 75-minute life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:12.720 --> 00:44:18.000
followed by a death that lasts until he&nbsp;
is rewound by a special key means that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:23.520
is easily contained and has been classified as&nbsp;
safe he is only to be activated during routine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:23.520 --> 00:44:28.800
testing and After experiencing death he is to&nbsp;
be placed back into his coffin along with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:33.480
key in keeping with current regulations for all&nbsp;
anomalies that have been designated as misters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:34.020 --> 00:44:40.740
scp-1007 is to be contained in Hall 8 of&nbsp;
site 13 for additional observation and study

00:44:47.160 --> 00:44:53.580
some of the anomalies the SCP Foundation deals&nbsp;
with are dangerous with the most powerful able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:53.580 --> 00:44:59.880
to end all life and even reality as we know it&nbsp;
others pose no threat at all and seem content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:07.140
to Simply exist still others are something&nbsp;
else entirely scp-49999 is a humanoid entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:07.140 --> 00:45:12.180
though its appearance seems to fluctuate between&nbsp;
manifestations with the only unchanging detail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:12.180 --> 00:45:16.920
being that it always is dressed in dark Formal&nbsp;
Wear originally thought by many to be an urban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:16.920 --> 00:45:23.640
legend local Tales of scp-4999 are what initially&nbsp;
tipped the foundation off to its existence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:28.620
further Research indicates that there are accounts&nbsp;
that may be referring to the appearances of 49.99&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:28.620 --> 00:45:33.360
throughout recorded history strangest of&nbsp;
all though is the consistency with which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:33.360 --> 00:45:39.240
it appears or rather the consistent situations&nbsp;
and types of people it appears to from the data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:39.240 --> 00:45:45.840
available it seems that scp-4999 only appears&nbsp;
to people in a very specific type of need as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:51.480
you'll see in the case of a subject named Alex&nbsp;
hiriford and the Fateful Knight he experienced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:57.000
the road was slippery and Alex was driving too&nbsp;
fast he knew this of course but it's a different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:57.000 --> 00:46:01.260
matter altogether to know a thing and to and&nbsp;
to care about it rain hammered on the front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:01.260 --> 00:46:07.260
windshield the weak headlights of his 2005 Honda&nbsp;
Civic barely punching into the thick black knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:07.260 --> 00:46:12.420
ahead of him winding through the Mountainside&nbsp;
the road was mostly empty saved for the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:12.420 --> 00:46:17.820
occasional twin beams of light blazing past him&nbsp;
due to his high speed it was hard to hear the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:23.880
honking of angry horns over the heavy pounding of&nbsp;
the rain then it happened in a way Alex knew it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:23.880 --> 00:46:29.400
was inevitable his tread worn Wheels finally lost&nbsp;
contact with the ground thick layer of rain water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:29.400 --> 00:46:35.160
between them and asphalt betraying his speeding&nbsp;
Vehicles grip on the road and sending it careening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:35.160 --> 00:46:42.180
out of control he had expected fear but instead&nbsp;
felt nothing really a slight sense of anticipation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:42.180 --> 00:46:47.760
like wincing right before a punch lands in that&nbsp;
childhood game of hitting each other on the arm it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:47.760 --> 00:46:53.220
wasn't that the world had slowed down but perhaps&nbsp;
his brain was simply working at a much greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:59.100
velocity now recognizing its own impending&nbsp;
death his speed of thought seemed magnified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:59.100 --> 00:47:04.680
to the point of slowing his perception down he&nbsp;
heard of soldiers in war zones experiencing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:04.680 --> 00:47:10.440
same phenomenon as they felt sure that in the next&nbsp;
few seconds they'd be dead Alex Wonder would he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:10.440 --> 00:47:16.140
smash into a tree go off a Cliff's Edge you could&nbsp;
hardly see the forest or the terrain Beyond in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:16.140 --> 00:47:21.420
thick rain in the dark of the mountain though he&nbsp;
traveled this road a million times before he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:21.420 --> 00:47:26.880
no idea where he actually was tonight he supposed&nbsp;
it wouldn't really matter which it was as usual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:26.880 --> 00:47:32.040
his thoughts turned to her or rather they had&nbsp;
simply run their course and return to the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:32.040 --> 00:47:36.780
place they always did it wasn't like there were&nbsp;
many other people to think about in Alex's mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:36.780 --> 00:47:43.620
empty life there was and always had been since&nbsp;
the moment he'd met her mostly just her but even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:43.620 --> 00:47:48.660
Alex's heightened State of Mind couldn't delay&nbsp;
the inevitable for long it would be a cliff after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:48.660 --> 00:47:55.320
all Alex thought curiously catching a glimpse of&nbsp;
town lights far away and below the correspond 180&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:55.320 --> 00:48:01.320
degrees out into empty air Then Came Crashing&nbsp;
Down with a horror Roar of shattered glass and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:01.320 --> 00:48:06.960
tearing metal as it tumbled down the hillside even&nbsp;
over the torrential downpour the noise of Alex's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:06.960 --> 00:48:12.660
crash was significant had anyone been around to&nbsp;
hear it finally after over a hundred feet down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:12.660 --> 00:48:18.780
a steep incline the car smashed into a single&nbsp;
thick oak tree bringing the disaster to an end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:18.780 --> 00:48:25.680
as if On Cue the rain began to let up slowly at&nbsp;
first then all of a sudden in that peculiar way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:25.680 --> 00:48:31.800
that Northwest torrential downpours tend to do as&nbsp;
if the sky had at last finished emptying itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:31.800 --> 00:48:39.900
all at once inside the shattered vehicle Alex was&nbsp;
incredibly alive at least for the time being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:39.900 --> 00:48:44.940
airbag deployment had spared his face the worst&nbsp;
of it and the sturdy aluminum frame of the vehicle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:44.940 --> 00:48:50.700
had given its all in protecting Alex's body from&nbsp;
the downhill crash but even post-modern vehicle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:50.700 --> 00:48:57.840
engineering had its limits his breath came in&nbsp;
slow ragged gasps difficult at first but gradually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:57.840 --> 00:49:03.720
steady not an Improvement in his condition but&nbsp;
rather his body dedicating the rapidly dwindling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:03.720 --> 00:49:10.020
resources at its disposal into keeping vital&nbsp;
functions going as long as possible opening his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:10.020 --> 00:49:15.480
eyes Alex was surprised to find himself right side&nbsp;
up less surprised to look down at the shattered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:15.480 --> 00:49:22.200
mess his Limbs and lower body had become gradually&nbsp;
Alex's thoughts clear his sense of self returning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:22.200 --> 00:49:27.480
after the bone jarring dropped down the Steep&nbsp;
incline and sudden stop at the end looking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:32.520
his right he could see the trunk of the tree that&nbsp;
had stopped his out-of-control Temple despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:32.520 --> 00:49:39.960
himself Alex laugh a weak gurgling chuckle so&nbsp;
it was the cliff and a tree after all he focused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:39.960 --> 00:49:45.180
on breathing letting the waves of pain wash over&nbsp;
him until his brain eventually canceled them out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:45.180 --> 00:49:51.120
by injecting his broken body with adrenaline and&nbsp;
chemicals everything was quiet and still after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:57.900
crash and the rain but to his surprise he could&nbsp;
hear something it was faint at first just a soft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:57.900 --> 00:50:04.620
crunch of footsteps on grab but the sound grew&nbsp;
louder and louder until at last it came to a stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:04.620 --> 00:50:10.620
outside Alex's window with every ounce of effort&nbsp;
Alex turned his head towards the sound a rescuer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:10.620 --> 00:50:16.080
now impossible nobody was up on this mountain&nbsp;
and nobody could possibly have reached him here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:16.080 --> 00:50:21.240
so quickly even if there had been he supposed&nbsp;
he should have been surprised yet almost from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:21.240 --> 00:50:26.760
the moment that his eyes fell on the tall handsome&nbsp;
figure with the Casual yet fashionably cut black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:26.760 --> 00:50:33.420
suit Alex accepted him for what he was there was&nbsp;
no shock no confusion for the second time tonight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:33.420 --> 00:50:40.440
just a calm sense of acceptance the man probably&nbsp;
somewhere in his mid-30s leaned down to peer in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:40.440 --> 00:50:46.200
through the window he said nothing as he casually&nbsp;
observed the extent of Alex's injuries satisfied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:51.840
he laid a hand on Alex's shoulder the grip was&nbsp;
firm but not painfully so just strong enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:51.840 --> 00:50:57.300
to communicate I am here with you things will&nbsp;
be all right after a slight squeeze the figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:57.300 --> 00:51:02.640
reached inside his jacket and produced a pack of&nbsp;
cigarettes packing the tobacco with swift Taps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:02.640 --> 00:51:08.640
against his palm before removing two cigarettes&nbsp;
and offering one to Alex Alex nodded his head a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:08.640 --> 00:51:14.040
very small motion that exploded pain across his&nbsp;
shattered body now thank you but that stuff will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:14.040 --> 00:51:20.040
kill you Alex smiled the man paused for a moment&nbsp;
the ghost of a smile showing on his face for just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:25.440
a moment before disappearing returning the offered&nbsp;
cigarette the man took his own and lit it giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:25.440 --> 00:51:30.480
Alex a good look at his face in the light of his&nbsp;
cigarette lighter Alex had been right the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:30.480 --> 00:51:36.780
appeared to be somewhere in his mid to late 30s&nbsp;
