02:52:22.500 --> 02:52:29.040
gear shift handbrake and pedals all functioned&nbsp;
exactly the same one look at the outer panels of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:29.040 --> 02:52:35.279
the Microbus would have told you what it was and&nbsp;
where it was heading the word Starmobile was spray&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:35.279 --> 02:52:41.279
painted on one side side and the other Alpha&nbsp;
Centauri or Bust the 4th of July rolled around&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:41.279 --> 02:52:47.399
and their Starmobile took flight William keeping a&nbsp;
diary of their Journey referred to himself and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:47.399 --> 02:52:53.819
friends as the only four people in the universe&nbsp;
who were truly free careening upwards at 82 miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:53.819 --> 02:53:00.000
per hour without any police to stop them no longer&nbsp;
restricted by mundane life on Earth the group&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:00.000 --> 02:53:06.600
traveled higher and higher in their Microbus their&nbsp;
plan was to travel straight to Alpha Centauri the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:06.600 --> 02:53:12.300
closest star and planetary system to our own solar&nbsp;
system thinking their Journey would only last&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:12.300 --> 02:53:18.720
a few short weeks William and his friends waved&nbsp;
farewell to Earth the bus had everything on board&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:18.720 --> 02:53:24.720
that these Intergalactic Travelers could possibly&nbsp;
need from bedrolls and pillows to sleep on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:24.720 --> 02:53:30.240
enough dehydrated food to feed the four of them&nbsp;
for three whole months in space there was even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:30.240 --> 02:53:36.479
room aboard the Microbus for Susan's cat Millie as&nbsp;
well as all the Comforts of Home William and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:36.479 --> 02:53:43.019
friends packed Bongos a guitar and countless books&nbsp;
but this road trip wasn't just an aimless Joyride&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:43.020 --> 02:53:49.800
out into the cosmos the Intrepid group had enough&nbsp;
supplies with them and enough ambition to set up&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:49.800 --> 02:53:55.680
the first off-world human Colony they'd practice&nbsp;
seed bank containing hundreds if not thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:55.680 --> 02:54:01.380
of varying seeds from a number of common domestic&nbsp;
plants from Earth on top of that there were even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:01.380 --> 02:54:08.399
Frozen egg cells of domestic animals like cats and&nbsp;
dogs and livestocks such as cows and pigs these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:08.399 --> 02:54:13.679
embryos were all ready to be unfrozen and allowed&nbsp;
to grow once the gang reached their destination&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:13.680 --> 02:54:19.140
however it didn't take long for problems to&nbsp;
start arising for one the group quickly ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:19.140 --> 02:54:24.779
out of Libations within the first five days of&nbsp;
leaving Earth Spirits were naturally dampened by&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:24.779 --> 02:54:30.540
the absence of spirits but William tried to remain&nbsp;
optimistic hoping to grow barley and concoct&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:30.540 --> 02:54:36.359
some homemade Brew once they arrived at Alpha&nbsp;
Centauri but while the lack of Ale and lager was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:36.359 --> 02:54:43.019
an inconvenience there was worse on the horizon&nbsp;
during a group sing-along something collided with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:43.020 --> 02:54:48.359
the Starmobile naturally All Aboard were rattled&nbsp;
and it was Jerry who stepped up to calm everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:48.359 --> 02:54:54.779
stating it was likely just space dust or debris&nbsp;
he opted to take a look outside and see if there&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:54.779 --> 02:55:00.719
had been any damage to the Microbus donning a&nbsp;
homemade spacesuit Jerry left via the airlock&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:00.720 --> 02:55:06.120
at the rear of the bus and examined finding no&nbsp;
significant harm had been done but as he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:06.120 --> 02:55:12.059
about to make his way back inside something struck&nbsp;
the Starmobile again the force of it caused Jerry&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:12.060 --> 02:55:17.520
to lose his grip sending him drifting out into&nbsp;
space William was the only one at the wheel of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:17.520 --> 02:55:23.700
the bus but had never learned to drive eventually&nbsp;
he was able to turn the samba bus around but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:23.700 --> 02:55:30.899
was too late Jerry was dead adrift in the cold&nbsp;
vacuum the loss overwhelmed the group but hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:30.899 --> 02:55:37.019
Susan worst of all she and Jerry had wanted to get&nbsp;
married the moment they arrived at Alpha Centauri&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:37.020 --> 02:55:41.760
William had even obtained a Minister's license&nbsp;
so he could officiate his friend's wedding that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:41.760 --> 02:55:47.220
would now never happen three days later Sam and&nbsp;
William awoke to find Susan dead on the floor of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:47.220 --> 02:55:53.399
the bus the grief and sorrow had gotten too much&nbsp;
for her according to William's diary she died of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:53.399 --> 02:55:59.339
a broken heart drawing up his guitar and strumming&nbsp;
Amazing Grace for his second dead friend William&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:59.340 --> 02:56:04.740
watched as Sam let Susan's body drift out of the&nbsp;
airlock he wrote In This Journal that he hoped&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:04.740 --> 02:56:10.679
she would find Jerry out there in space and at&nbsp;
least they would be together by now it had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:10.680 --> 02:56:16.859
well over 50 days since the Starmobile had left&nbsp;
the safe confines of planet Earth the group had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:16.859 --> 02:56:23.040
suffered two tragic heartbreaking casualties&nbsp;
already one by accident and one as a result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:23.040 --> 02:56:28.979
the first and yet William and Sam the survivors&nbsp;
were still traveling even deeper into the Dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:28.979 --> 02:56:35.160
Void above plotting their chorus to Alpha Centauri&nbsp;
as best they could with the hand-drawn Star Charts&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:35.160 --> 02:56:40.319
they had brought with Femme so far their journey&nbsp;
into space had begun with promise and optimism&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:40.319 --> 02:56:47.759
and was now fraught with dangers and obstacles and&nbsp;
these were far from over slowly William began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:47.760 --> 02:56:52.500
realize that it was taking much longer to reach&nbsp;
their destination than he and Jerry had first&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:52.500 --> 02:56:58.140
anticipated Alpha centauri's roughly four and a&nbsp;
half light years from Earth bear in mind that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:58.140 --> 02:57:02.880
single light year is equivalent to roughly&nbsp;
6 trillion miles William was unsure if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:02.880 --> 02:57:08.340
Microbus had been traveling in the right direction&nbsp;
or if it had even managed to miss the Terminus of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:08.340 --> 02:57:14.100
the journey the charts Jerry had drawn were of&nbsp;
little help he had been the expert the one who&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:14.100 --> 02:57:19.979
planned the trip and modified the Volkswagen Type&nbsp;
2 Samba bus for space travel William was out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:19.979 --> 02:57:25.379
his depth hurtling through the Galaxy with Little&nbsp;
Help from his passenger to make matters worse&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:25.380 --> 02:57:31.319
both William and Sam had started feeling unwell&nbsp;
not just travel sick as you might expect after&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:31.319 --> 02:57:36.599
spending a long ride in the Microbus trundling&nbsp;
through space their illness wasn't even caused by&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:36.600 --> 02:57:42.359
being trapped in the cramped space for such a long&nbsp;
duration of time blotches had begun to appear all&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:42.359 --> 02:57:48.479
over their skin and Sam had been having trouble&nbsp;
eating at random even a tooth spontaneously fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:48.479 --> 02:57:54.419
out of his mouth these aren't symptoms typical&nbsp;
of space travel though due to a severe lack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:54.420 --> 02:58:00.240
vitamin C in the food they had packed the pair&nbsp;
of them had developed scurvy just as it seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:00.240 --> 02:58:05.399
like a trip to Alpha Centauri couldn't have been a&nbsp;
bigger disaster William awoke to see something out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:05.399 --> 02:58:11.339
of the Microbus window something he had probably&nbsp;
seen hundreds of times in his lifetime but seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:11.340 --> 02:58:19.560
it now filled him with dread it was the moon as&nbsp;
in Earth's Moon they were barely close to Alpha&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:19.560 --> 02:58:24.359
Centauri quickly realizing that they would never&nbsp;
reach their destination on their current course&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:24.359 --> 02:58:30.420
due to their Grievous errors in calculation&nbsp;
William did the only thing he could he closed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:30.420 --> 02:58:36.479
the curtains so that Sam couldn't see how big of&nbsp;
a mistake they had made eventually Millie crawled&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:36.479 --> 02:58:42.120
behind the sofa and died meanwhile Sam stopped&nbsp;
being able to keep his food down towards the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:42.120 --> 02:58:47.760
he could barely so much as see or even sit every&nbsp;
time he asked his friend if they had arrived yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:47.760 --> 02:58:53.160
William would tell him that they would be there&nbsp;
tomorrow he couldn't bring himself to tell Sam&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:53.160 --> 02:59:00.899
the truth finally Sam asked William to read to him&nbsp;
a poem by Dylan Thomas called and Death Shall Have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:00.899 --> 02:59:07.319
No Dominion he was dead before William finished&nbsp;
reading saddened and filled with remorse William&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:07.319 --> 02:59:12.779
pushed the last of his friends out of the airlock&nbsp;
realizing that no one would be left to push him&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:12.779 --> 02:59:18.479
out whenever he eventually died the final thought&nbsp;
he recorded in his diary came after two whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:18.479 --> 02:59:24.599
months spent isolated and alone in space before&nbsp;
William's death the last thing he wrote was that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:24.600 --> 02:59:30.300
the Stars looked so beautiful against the dark&nbsp;
backdrop of the universe in spite of the tragedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:30.300 --> 02:59:38.640
of his situation so few others especially from his&nbsp;
time would ever truly see them like this today the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:38.640 --> 02:59:45.840
bus is still drifting quietly through space now&nbsp;
known as scp-1958 it rests in the orbit of Mars&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:45.840 --> 02:59:51.960
the withered remains of its driver still sitting&nbsp;
at the wheel William and his friends never made it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:51.960 --> 02:59:58.319
to Alpha Centauri in fact it would have taken them&nbsp;
almost 40 million years to reach it they never&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:58.319 --> 03:00:06.359
saw their dream come to the ending that they had&nbsp;
planned instead William Jerry Sam Susan and Millie&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:06.359 --> 03:00:14.460
the cat all died Among the Stars driving their&nbsp;
magic bus their Starmobile out into the unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:14.460 --> 03:00:24.779
for them space that final frontier had a lot more&nbsp;
finality to it water the Wellspring of Life we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:24.779 --> 03:00:31.139
dealt with a number of anomalous water sources on&nbsp;
this channel like scp-006 the much sought after&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:31.140 --> 03:00:38.100
Fountain of Youth or the terrifying scp-3280&nbsp;
where murderous water threatens to destroy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:38.100 --> 03:00:44.700
entire world but we've never seen anomalous water&nbsp;
that behaves quite like this before in many of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:44.700 --> 03:00:50.700
legends of King Arthur the sword of Excalibur is&nbsp;
presented to him by the mystical Lady of the Lake&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:50.700 --> 03:00:57.120
this lady emerges from the depths of the water&nbsp;
gifting Arthur with the enchanted sword it's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:57.120 --> 03:01:03.840
incredible if impossible image a woman appearing&nbsp;
from within the lake rising up from the bottom and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:03.840 --> 03:01:08.880
breaking through the surface it's safe to say&nbsp;
that none of us have ever seen anything quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:08.880 --> 03:01:15.180
like it well at least most of us haven't in a&nbsp;
small unnamed English Village there was a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:15.180 --> 03:01:21.300
woman who set out on a particularly lovely warm&nbsp;
spring day to take a swim in a nearby lake while&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:21.300 --> 03:01:27.060
waiting in the water enjoying the sunlight and the&nbsp;
gentle breeze on her skin she saw a strange Ripple&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:27.060 --> 03:01:33.479
ghost across the surface she stopped her swimming&nbsp;
staring at the motion she expected to spot a fish&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:33.479 --> 03:01:40.500
or some other aquatic creature instead the water&nbsp;
itself began to rise up Gathering and forming&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:40.500 --> 03:01:48.300
into a shape before her eyes it was impossible and&nbsp;
yet here it was happening she pinched herself and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:48.300 --> 03:01:54.240
found that she was definitely awake as the water&nbsp;
transformed into the shape of a human woman it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:54.240 --> 03:02:00.420
turned to look at her shimmering eyes finding hers&nbsp;
and liquid lips forming into a warm inviting smile&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:00.420 --> 03:02:07.439
though this being was shocking to see it clearly&nbsp;
meant her no harm it raised a translucent arm and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:07.439 --> 03:02:12.719
gave her a small wave as if to welcome her to&nbsp;
its home the young woman approached this Lady&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:12.720 --> 03:02:18.600
of the Lake reaching out her own hand of Flesh&nbsp;
and bone to touch this Impossible Creature just&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:18.600 --> 03:02:23.580
as her fingertips reached the water woman's own&nbsp;
the figure dissolved back into the lake with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:23.580 --> 03:02:29.040
splash the young woman ran home telling anyone&nbsp;
who would listen about the incredible thing she&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:29.040 --> 03:02:34.620
had seen that day of course no one believed her&nbsp;
that is until word of her sighting reached the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:34.620 --> 03:02:41.340
only people who might take her claim seriously the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation they sent operatives to the lake&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:41.340 --> 03:02:48.060
where they managed to capture the shape-shifting&nbsp;
entity dwelling there scp-054 also known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:48.060 --> 03:02:53.880
water nymph is a being made up entirely of water&nbsp;
with an average volume of 90 liters when it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:53.880 --> 03:02:59.160
out of a body of water the being tends to adopt&nbsp;
the appearance of a humanoid woman though it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:59.160 --> 03:03:04.559
capable of taking on a variety of other shapes&nbsp;
including other humanoids animals and various&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:04.560 --> 03:03:09.960
inanimate objects The Entity is also capable of&nbsp;
shedding its form and effectively disappearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:09.960 --> 03:03:15.000
into a given body of water in order to avoid&nbsp;
shrinking or possibly disappearing entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:15.000 --> 03:03:22.260
from evaporation scp-054 is required to return&nbsp;
to a larger body of water studies of samples&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:22.260 --> 03:03:27.660
taken from the entity's body or its version of&nbsp;
a body revealed that it is made up of ordinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:27.660 --> 03:03:34.019
water there is no apparent reason for its ability&nbsp;
to move and no thermal electromagnetic biological&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:34.020 --> 03:03:39.120
or Supernatural anomalies where were detected the&nbsp;
research team could not determine what might make&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:39.120 --> 03:03:44.939
this water alive and sentient and the nature of&nbsp;
its unusual properties is uncertain to this day&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:44.939 --> 03:03:51.719
when scp-054 was first brought into containment&nbsp;
at site-08 it displayed surprisingly congenial&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:51.720 --> 03:03:57.180
and curious Behavior often walking around outside&nbsp;
of the water and taking turns mimicking the shapes&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:57.180 --> 03:04:02.640
of various staff and scientists that spoke to it&nbsp;
its demeanor began to shift towards suspicion and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:02.640 --> 03:04:07.200
aggression however following a series of&nbsp;
experiments and an incident involving the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:07.200 --> 03:04:13.019
research staff the first experiment conducted on&nbsp;
scp-054 sought to determine what would happen if&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:13.020 --> 03:04:17.160
the entity was denied access to any fresh&nbsp;
water water was drained from the fountain&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:17.160 --> 03:04:22.139
holding it leaving only enough water for it to&nbsp;
form a humanoid shape but no additional water&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:22.140 --> 03:04:28.380
in the base and to compensate for the effects&nbsp;
of evaporation over time scp-054 became visibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:28.380 --> 03:04:32.700
frustrated as the water was being drained&nbsp;
out of its enclosure for the next few days&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:32.700 --> 03:04:37.439
it enthusiastically greeted anyone who entered&nbsp;
its contain attainment facility attempting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:37.439 --> 03:04:42.779
use a report and sense of familiarity to convince&nbsp;
the person to provide it with more water after it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:42.779 --> 03:04:47.160
realized that this approach had no impact on&nbsp;
the amount of water in its Fountain it became&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:47.160 --> 03:04:52.680
distant and even cold to anyone who attempted&nbsp;
to speak to it 054 only became friendly again&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:52.680 --> 03:04:58.680
once the water in its Fountain was restored to a&nbsp;
pre-experiment level next the research team opted&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:58.680 --> 03:05:05.640
to test scp-054's reaction to extreme temperatures&nbsp;
particularly extreme cold the temperature of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:05.640 --> 03:05:10.859
containment facility was slowly dropped until the&nbsp;
room fell below the freezing point of water as&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:10.859 --> 03:05:16.859
the temperature dropped 054 became sluggish and&nbsp;
exhausted it lost its ability to shift between&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:16.859 --> 03:05:23.040
forms remaining locked in its preferred humanoid&nbsp;
female shape its movement slowed more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:23.040 --> 03:05:28.500
as the room grew colder until the entity was&nbsp;
completely frozen solid portions of the ice were&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:28.500 --> 03:05:33.720
chipped off and studied revealing the crystals&nbsp;
were identical to those of ordinary ice after&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:33.720 --> 03:05:38.640
the Sub-Zero testing the re research team decided&nbsp;
to take things to the other end of the spectrum&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:38.640 --> 03:05:44.880
and test the effects of heat on scp-054 the&nbsp;
subject was placed in a tank outfitted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:44.880 --> 03:05:49.740
heating equipment and its temperature was slowly&nbsp;
raised over the course of several minutes when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:49.740 --> 03:05:54.359
water reached a temperature of 95 degrees&nbsp;
the entity's behavior became frenetic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:54.359 --> 03:05:59.399
aggressive it pounded on the glass walls of the&nbsp;
tank and attempted to break through the lid in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:59.399 --> 03:06:04.740
desperate bid for escape until the temperature was&nbsp;
returned to a comfortable level after the extreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:04.740 --> 03:06:10.200
temperature experiments the previous column&nbsp;
and Cooperative nature of scp-054 was nowhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:10.200 --> 03:06:15.240
to be found this subject displayed increased&nbsp;
suspicion of the research team and would fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:15.240 --> 03:06:20.399
back whenever it was removed from its Fountain&nbsp;
and taken to a lab for experimentation in spite&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:20.399 --> 03:06:25.679
of this newfound resistance the team decided to&nbsp;
continue their experiments as planned hoping that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:25.680 --> 03:06:31.500
the entity would return to its formerly docile&nbsp;
self over time next Dr seskel the acting head&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:31.500 --> 03:06:37.680
of the research team conducted a study involving&nbsp;
scp-054's memory and ability to be conditioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:37.680 --> 03:06:43.080
The Entity was presented with a series of&nbsp;
increasingly complex mazes and puzzles when&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:43.080 --> 03:06:48.120
it failed to comply with the experiment or solved&nbsp;
a puzzle incorrectly The Entity was punished with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:48.120 --> 03:06:53.340
an electrical shock or the release of silica&nbsp;
gel into its body both of these options seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:53.340 --> 03:06:58.680
to cause it a great deal of pain and distress&nbsp;
and it was eager to avoid further exposure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:58.680 --> 03:07:04.439
them scp-054 displayed impressive learning&nbsp;
and problem-solving capabilities revealing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:04.439 --> 03:07:09.419
it is likely much more intelligent than it&nbsp;
was first presumed to be Dr seskel observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:09.420 --> 03:07:14.100
the experiments and with the effectiveness of&nbsp;
his somewhat unsavory motivational techniques&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:14.100 --> 03:07:19.740
quipped to his research assistant that they would&nbsp;
have it trained to fetch in no time after several&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:19.740 --> 03:07:24.719
days of these experiments and repeated use of&nbsp;
both the silica gel and electrical shocks the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:24.720 --> 03:07:29.880
entity's progress slowed down considerably and&nbsp;
it became visibly exhausted it was removed from&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:29.880 --> 03:07:35.220
the lab for a 48-hour rest period before&nbsp;
experimentation was resumed yet again this&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:35.220 --> 03:07:42.060
Time Dr seskel planned to expose scp-054's water&nbsp;
source to various levels of acids and bases&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:42.060 --> 03:07:48.000
in order to test its homeostatic capabilities&nbsp;
beginning with a 0.5 M solution of hydrochloric&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:48.000 --> 03:07:54.479
acid prior to conducting the experiment Dr seskel&nbsp;
noted I have no idea what will happen but if this&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:54.479 --> 03:08:00.299
thing incorporates homeostatic mechanisms like&nbsp;
I suspect then we should get some insight into&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:00.300 --> 03:08:06.060
how it maintains its form he also noted that&nbsp;
scp-054's behavior was becoming increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:06.060 --> 03:08:12.120
erratic but made the decision to continue with&nbsp;
the experiment as planned scp-054 displayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:12.120 --> 03:08:16.439
a now familiar reluctance when it was removed&nbsp;
from its containment chamber and taken to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:16.439 --> 03:08:21.479
lab it thrashed around in the fountain splashing&nbsp;
researchers with water and retreated from them&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:21.479 --> 03:08:26.279
as they approached in spite of its efforts&nbsp;
however it was removed from its Fountain and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:26.279 --> 03:08:31.380
placed in the experimental tank the solution of&nbsp;
hydrochloric acid was then dripped into the tank&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:31.380 --> 03:08:38.040
and then all hell broke loose as soon as the&nbsp;
acid touched the surface of its water scp-054&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:38.040 --> 03:08:44.100
became incredibly distressed it Formed into the&nbsp;
shape of a human face eyes wide mouth open in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:44.100 --> 03:08:48.660
a Silent Scream Of Rage and pain the water&nbsp;
churned so aggressively that the lid of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:48.660 --> 03:08:53.939
tank was shaken loose allowing it to escape the&nbsp;
