anomalies the SCP Foundation has ever come across&nbsp;
perhaps he was a deeply Disturbed World War one&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:42.000 --> 03:25:48.000
soldier who gazed too long into something better&nbsp;
left untouched perhaps he was never human at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:48.000 --> 03:25:53.160
but instead a Divergent humanoid species&nbsp;
that preyed on early prehistoric mankind&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:53.160 --> 03:26:00.840
today we're focusing on the third possibility and&nbsp;
arguably the most tragic of the three it begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:00.840 --> 03:26:07.319
with another man we've covered on the channel&nbsp;
before named Dr Robert Scranton and his wife Dr&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:07.319 --> 03:26:13.500
Anna Lang you probably know them for two things&nbsp;
the Scranton reality anchor and The Accidental&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:13.500 --> 03:26:20.340
discovery of scp-3001 or the red reality in case&nbsp;
you haven't seen our video on the subject here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:20.340 --> 03:26:27.359
a brief recap of the whole unfortunate affair&nbsp;
on January 2nd 2000 at site 120 Robert and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:27.359 --> 03:26:31.799
Anna were hard at work as the head researchers&nbsp;
developing an experimental device known as The&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:31.800 --> 03:26:38.460
Lang Scranton stabilizer the LSS was intended to&nbsp;
work as a reality anchor but it was in its early&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:38.460 --> 03:26:45.660
stages and still unstable a seismic event rocked&nbsp;
the research site damaging several LSS units and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:45.660 --> 03:26:50.279
creating a wormhole that transported Dr Scranton&nbsp;
to the pocket Dimension Hereafter referred to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:50.279 --> 03:26:59.519
as scp-3001 this little pocket of space this&nbsp;
impossible world just adjacent to ours has some&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:59.520 --> 03:27:05.760
unusual properties it causes matter within it to&nbsp;
deteriorate as its Hume level approaches that of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:05.760 --> 03:27:11.760
the environment Humes being the measurement unit&nbsp;
for reality stability Robert Scranton was trapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:11.760 --> 03:27:19.439
there in the red reality alive for a terrifyingly&nbsp;
long time five years 11 months and 21 days before&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:19.439 --> 03:27:26.339
the logs he kept ended there he struggled to hold&nbsp;
on to himself he grasped desperately at shreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:26.340 --> 03:27:33.660
his Humanity his memories even as the world around&nbsp;
him slowly ate them away finally only one thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:33.660 --> 03:27:41.220
remained Anna wife he could just barely remember&nbsp;
her name remember that he wanted to get back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:41.220 --> 03:27:47.760
her there was a brief moment of Hope on December&nbsp;
23 2005 when the LSS control panel reappeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:47.760 --> 03:27:54.660
a Testing Lab at site 120. Dr Anna Lang arrived&nbsp;
to monitor the situation a massive bloody organic&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:54.660 --> 03:28:00.000
matter appeared alongside it and as Anna called&nbsp;
out for her lost love something clattered to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:00.000 --> 03:28:05.640
floor and broke her heart her husband's wedding&nbsp;
ring stained with unidentified organic matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:05.640 --> 03:28:12.060
smelling of black blood and spoiled meat she&nbsp;
collapsed under the weight of the possibility that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:12.060 --> 03:28:19.020
her husband was no longer lost in a physical sense&nbsp;
but in another sense entirely that this mass of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:19.020 --> 03:28:25.859
Flesh unrecognizable as human might be the man she&nbsp;
once loved tying his favorite tie for him on date&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:25.859 --> 03:28:31.080
nights dancing drunkenly to Living on a Prayer&nbsp;
collapsing on the couch together breathless with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:31.080 --> 03:28:38.220
laughter and the sheer Joy of one another that he&nbsp;
could be both here here at last but Gone Forever&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:38.220 --> 03:28:43.739
Dr Anna Lang was taken to the medical Bay and&nbsp;
treated for shock years passed after Ana's last&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:43.739 --> 03:28:48.719
encounter with her husband she carried the ring&nbsp;
with her in her pocket every day for the first few&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:48.720 --> 03:28:54.239
after five years she threaded the chain through it&nbsp;
wearing it around her neck under her clothes after&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:54.239 --> 03:29:00.420
10 more years she stopped noticing it was even&nbsp;
on anymore it had become a part of her engraved&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:00.420 --> 03:29:06.779
on her heart with the memories of the man she had&nbsp;
loved lost and grieved with nothing to go home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:06.779 --> 03:29:12.719
at the end of the day no one to share her time off&nbsp;
with Anna began to pour herself deeper into her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:12.720 --> 03:29:19.319
work she would never remarry she knew that Robert&nbsp;
had been the only man for her now there was only&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:19.319 --> 03:29:24.960
her commitment to the foundation and the research&nbsp;
she did there and the silent promise she made to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:24.960 --> 03:29:31.140
herself that she would never let anything like the&nbsp;
events of January 2nd 2000 happen again but will&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:31.140 --> 03:29:36.960
they with no reason to go home honest nights at&nbsp;
the lab grew later and later her colleagues often&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:36.960 --> 03:29:42.359
joke that she might as well sleep there since that&nbsp;
was the only thing she went home to do the sadness&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:42.359 --> 03:29:47.279
behind her eyes tended to cut their jokes short&nbsp;
soon after making them though Anna liked the late&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:47.279 --> 03:29:53.700
night work the lab was still almost Serene she&nbsp;
could disappear into the research the calculations&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:53.700 --> 03:29:59.399
let them take over and quiet the noise in her&nbsp;
mind the lights were dimmed no one was asking&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:59.399 --> 03:30:04.979
her a name questions or bustling around while&nbsp;
she'd tried to focus there was nothing but her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:04.979 --> 03:30:11.099
notes and textbooks the light of her lone desk&nbsp;
lamp glowing softly in the dark and the work it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:11.100 --> 03:30:16.800
was one of these late nights buried in a mountain&nbsp;
of paperwork that Anna began to hear a strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:16.800 --> 03:30:23.460
sound she didn't notice it at first absorbed as&nbsp;
she was in a sea of calculations but soon it began&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:23.460 --> 03:30:30.779
to permeate the room breaking through her focus&nbsp;
a rustling sound a crackling of sorts quietly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:30.779 --> 03:30:36.359
murmuring into her ears though she was vaguely&nbsp;
aware of it the way you might be aware of the wind&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:36.359 --> 03:30:42.000
rustling through the trees outside your bedroom&nbsp;
window she didn't truly hear it until she smelled&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:42.000 --> 03:30:49.380
something faint but foul it was no matter how&nbsp;
muted the unmistakable scent of rot she stepped&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:49.380 --> 03:30:53.700
down from her lab stool her joints creaking&nbsp;
with effort as she worked out the stiffness&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:53.700 --> 03:30:59.279
in her muscles she adjusted her glasses peering&nbsp;
into the shadows for the source of the sound but&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:30:59.279 --> 03:31:04.979
saw nothing of note she took a step forward into&nbsp;
the dark then another and then another behind her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:04.979 --> 03:31:10.859
the desk lamp flickered then cut out entirely she&nbsp;
stopped blinking in the sudden complete darkness&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:10.859 --> 03:31:18.540
and sudden silence the noise had stopped the only&nbsp;
sound was her breathing quickened with fear she&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:18.540 --> 03:31:23.100
pulled the phone from her pocket and turned on&nbsp;
its flashlight using its weak beam to light her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:23.100 --> 03:31:28.260
way she turned back to her desk looking for the&nbsp;
issue that caused the light to cut out perhaps a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:28.260 --> 03:31:33.120
short in the wire or a bulb that needed changing&nbsp;
before she could take a look at the lamp however&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:33.120 --> 03:31:39.779
something else caught her eye there was something&nbsp;
slick and red on her stack of papers dripping onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:39.779 --> 03:31:45.960
the clean white surface and staining it with Gore&nbsp;
a closer look revealed what it was and a shiver&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:45.960 --> 03:31:53.520
ran down her spine a kidney fresh and human she&nbsp;
couldn't bring herself to touch it but somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:53.520 --> 03:31:58.920
knew that if she did it would be warm her heart&nbsp;
pounding and her suddenly tightening chest as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:31:58.920 --> 03:32:05.340
noise resumed behind her wet slapping louder than&nbsp;
before her feet moved on their own accord as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:05.340 --> 03:32:10.680
walked toward the sound holding the flashlight in&nbsp;
front of her in a shaking hand the black wall of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:10.680 --> 03:32:16.680
the lab illuminated by the light was smeared with&nbsp;
something dark and strange slick like oil but with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:16.680 --> 03:32:22.260
a rotten smell a closer look revealed that the&nbsp;
wall itself was beginning to change drooping&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:22.260 --> 03:32:28.500
limply like wet cardboard she froze watching&nbsp;
helplessly as the wall bubbled crumbling to Pieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:28.500 --> 03:32:35.220
suddenly a hand emerged from the wall gray skin&nbsp;
slick with black fluid its fingers surprisingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:35.220 --> 03:32:40.979
strong gripped her arm she tore it away scrambling&nbsp;
back and saw that pieces of her lab coat had come&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:40.979 --> 03:32:46.439
off melting into the gray skin of the alien hand&nbsp;
as the arm reached for her again she stumbled and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:46.439 --> 03:32:51.540
dropped her phone on the floor casting its light&nbsp;
against the wall and the figure warming its way&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:32:51.540 --> 03:33:00.120
out there it was an old man naked and gray with&nbsp;
slimy decaying skin coming off in pieces its&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:00.120 --> 03:33:05.580
throat was shredded an open wound and it grinned&nbsp;
at her with stiff shriveled lips stretched over&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:05.580 --> 03:33:11.160
blackened teeth its eyes were the worst part&nbsp;
even admits the rest of the Walking Corpse&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:11.160 --> 03:33:16.620
they were almost like a man's they were correct&nbsp;
in shape and placement but they were wrong they&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:16.620 --> 03:33:22.080
were empty clouded over and void of any warmth&nbsp;
or Mercy as he stood there the ground beneath&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:22.080 --> 03:33:28.080
him began to dissipate melting into an oily puddle&nbsp;
that enveloped her phone and stuffed out its light&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:28.080 --> 03:33:34.140
there was only one thing left for Anna to do and&nbsp;
so she ran she turned and made a break for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:34.140 --> 03:33:39.359
lab doors lungs burn learning from the effort&nbsp;
she cried out for the guard on night Duty Frank&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:39.359 --> 03:33:44.880
her voice was shrill and pleading he appeared from&nbsp;
around the corner gun already drawn eyes wide and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:44.880 --> 03:33:49.800
alert at the Panic he must have heard in her voice&nbsp;
as Frank tried to calm her down and she tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:49.800 --> 03:33:54.600
desperately to explain what she had seen the old&nbsp;
man forced his way through the lab doors leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:54.600 --> 03:33:59.939
a trail of corrosive black slime in his wake&nbsp;
Frank fired his gun hitting the old man in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:33:59.939 --> 03:34:05.700
chest twice he collapsed sinking into the floor&nbsp;
as his excretion broke away the tiles beneath him&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:05.700 --> 03:34:12.359
as Anna and Frank debated what to do next a drip&nbsp;
of black mucus landed on Frank's radio from above&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:12.359 --> 03:34:19.139
another drop fell Landing directly in his eye he&nbsp;
screamed in agony the mucus dissolving his eyeball&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:19.140 --> 03:34:24.899
on contact next the empty grin appeared through&nbsp;
the ceiling and the old man fell on top of Frank&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:24.899 --> 03:34:31.379
tearing out his throat with its bare hands Anna&nbsp;
knew that she had to escape but where could she&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:31.380 --> 03:34:38.760
go she couldn't think couldn't plan she just knew&nbsp;
she had to run she ran until her feet suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:38.760 --> 03:34:45.060
stopped obeying she was stuck she was sinking&nbsp;
into the ground and then she was falling down&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:45.060 --> 03:34:52.319
down into a moldy Dusty hallway dark except for a&nbsp;
nauseating greenish gray glow she had been pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:52.319 --> 03:34:58.500
into some new nightmarish world she ran through&nbsp;
a nearby door and found herself shockingly in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:34:58.500 --> 03:35:04.979
her old apartment how had she gotten here how did&nbsp;
the old man know this place there was her bed her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:04.979 --> 03:35:10.500
desk her closet she flung open the closet door&nbsp;
to find a pile of rotten corpses that poured out&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:10.500 --> 03:35:16.859
and slopped onto the floor she covered her mouth&nbsp;
to choke back a scream turned and fled then she&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:16.859 --> 03:35:25.080
was back in the hall this time she recognized it&nbsp;
it was a twisted warped version of sight 120. in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:25.080 --> 03:35:32.460
front of her there he was the old man had found&nbsp;
her again and now she was in his territory he&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:32.460 --> 03:35:41.279
stared at her with those Hollow eyes and for&nbsp;
the first time spoke he growled she stopped in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:35:41.279 --> 03:35:47.219
her tracks Frozen to the spot what he said next&nbsp;
turned her stomach and brought tears to her eyes

03:35:47.220 --> 03:35:53.520
he knew her name again he repeated

03:35:56.700 --> 03:36:03.239
he reached out to her with a hand that had a tan&nbsp;
line where a wedding ring had one spin the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:03.239 --> 03:36:09.540
ring burning against her skin under her shirt&nbsp;
he cupped her cheek and she felt the skin sting&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:09.540 --> 03:36:15.420
and blister he kissed her her teeth melting&nbsp;
infusing tongue turning to Mush but dribbled&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:15.420 --> 03:36:21.660
down her throat and choked her her last thought&nbsp;
through the fear and despair was the Egg of love&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:21.660 --> 03:36:30.840
her husband was not lost he was found and he had&nbsp;
found her too now they would be together forever&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:30.840 --> 03:36:37.859
not all heroes wear capes some of them wear&nbsp;
Pokemon t-shirts and a baseball cap you might&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:37.859 --> 03:36:43.679
think you've heard of every superhero out there&nbsp;
with Marvel and DC dominating the box office and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:43.680 --> 03:36:49.260
the incredible cactus man fighting crime on the&nbsp;
Mean Streets of Edinburgh but there is one tiny&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:49.260 --> 03:36:55.859
aspiring hero you'd likely never heard of in a&nbsp;
world filled with danger and evildoers one young&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:36:55.859 --> 03:37:03.479
boy armed with a a pure heart and some telekinetic&nbsp;
Powers dared to step up and save the day a woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:03.479 --> 03:37:09.419
was being abducted at gunpoint when seven-year-old&nbsp;
Cameron spotted the struggle he saw the weapon in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:09.420 --> 03:37:15.540
the man's hand the fear in the woman's eyes as she&nbsp;
looked for a way out and he knew that he had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:15.540 --> 03:37:20.939
act he concentrated with all his might reaching&nbsp;
out with his mind and threw the gun out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:20.939 --> 03:37:27.479
man's grasp and into some nearby bushes the woman&nbsp;
ran as fast as she could from there but not before&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:27.479 --> 03:37:33.599
catching a glimpse of the child that had saved&nbsp;
her life somehow she knew that he had been her&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:33.600 --> 03:37:39.840
hero unfortunately for Cameron but fortunately&nbsp;
for the SCP Foundation the woman reported what&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:39.840 --> 03:37:45.420
had happened to a nearby police officer who just&nbsp;
so happened to be an undercover agent for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:45.420 --> 03:37:51.479
foundation before Cameron could leave the scene he&nbsp;
was being approached by a team of armed guards and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:51.479 --> 03:37:58.799
brought to a strange new place filled with men&nbsp;
in lab coats who kept calling him as scp-2241&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:37:58.800 --> 03:38:04.920
Cameron sat for a very long time in a white room&nbsp;
wondering whether he was in trouble when a new man&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:04.920 --> 03:38:10.979
in a lab coat entered he introduced himself as&nbsp;
researcher Valdez and told Cameron he was going&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:10.979 --> 03:38:16.739
to ask him some questions he asked why Cameron&nbsp;
had helped the woman instead of running away and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:16.739 --> 03:38:22.679
getting an adult to help he said Superheroes have&nbsp;
to help people I can move things without touching&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:22.680 --> 03:38:27.420
them and other people can't so I should have used&nbsp;
that to help them he went on to explain that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:27.420 --> 03:38:33.000
had practiced his ability in the woods and kept&nbsp;
it a secret from everyone Valdez asked what sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:33.000 --> 03:38:38.220
of things Cameron could do and he explained I can&nbsp;
move stuff without touching it but not if it's too&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:38.220 --> 03:38:43.620
far away or if it's too big only like a cup across&nbsp;
the room or a person's arm or something sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:43.620 --> 03:38:49.739
I it can sort of change as well when prompted he&nbsp;
elaborated sometimes when I'm moving something it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:49.739 --> 03:38:53.700
changes to something I want like one time when&nbsp;
I was moving a stone it changed to look like&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:53.700 --> 03:38:58.800
a toy I lost but it changed back after a while&nbsp;
before I even got home Cameron became distressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:38:58.800 --> 03:39:03.600
during the interview but Valdez promised him&nbsp;
that he would be okay here he asked Cameron&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:03.600 --> 03:39:09.779
what his superhero name would be and he told&nbsp;
him Cameron the Crusader Valdez explained that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:09.779 --> 03:39:14.819
Cameron would be staying at the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
for a while so they could learn more about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:14.819 --> 03:39:21.239
powers and help him become a better superhero&nbsp;
researcher Valdez concluded his interview with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:21.239 --> 03:39:27.540
this closing statement scp-2241 appears to trust&nbsp;
me and believes that the foundation is attempting&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:27.540 --> 03:39:34.019
to help him as much as possible scp-2241's account&nbsp;
is consistent with the early stages of humanoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:34.020 --> 03:39:40.739
developing a reality bending ability scp-2241 may&nbsp;
have experienced abuse at the hands of its parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:40.739 --> 03:39:46.260
leading to early development of set ability in the&nbsp;
event that a more developed ability is required&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:46.260 --> 03:39:52.800
for research similar emotional stress can be&nbsp;
applied by Foundation staff scp-2241 is kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:52.800 --> 03:39:58.080
in a standard humanoid containment chamber he is&nbsp;
given access to television vision and comic books&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:39:58.080 --> 03:40:03.600
though this access can be cut off as punishment&nbsp;
for bad behavior he has fed three balanced meals&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:03.600 --> 03:40:09.000
a day with additional treats such as chocolate&nbsp;
or ice cream provided after testing especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:09.000 --> 03:40:14.880
if the testing goes on for a particularly long&nbsp;
time or is exceptionally stressful all Personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:14.880 --> 03:40:21.600
that interact with scp-2241 are to call him by&nbsp;
his name Cameron when interacting with him only&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:21.600 --> 03:40:27.540
Cameron's assigned psychologist and specifically&nbsp;
designated Personnel such as Valdez are allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:27.540 --> 03:40:33.120
to develop a friendly relationship with him if he&nbsp;
becomes attached to an unapproved person they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:33.120 --> 03:40:39.420
required to discourage this however they can after&nbsp;
containment procedures were established Valdez and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:39.420 --> 03:40:44.340
his team set to work putting together tests that&nbsp;
would use Cameron's emotions and desires to save&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:44.340 --> 03:40:49.260
people in order to develop and strengthen his&nbsp;
abilities for the first test they deliberately&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:49.260 --> 03:40:55.020
exposed Cameron to a d-class that believed him&nbsp;
to be a valuable hostage one that he could use&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:40:55.020 --> 03:41:00.000
to escape from the foundation the d-class&nbsp;
abducted Cameron at knife point but Cameron&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:00.000 --> 03:41:04.800
quickly used his reality bending ability to&nbsp;
turn the knife into chocolate and escape the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:04.800 --> 03:41:10.500
knife remained chocolate and did not turn back&nbsp;
to metal indicating his powers had grown stronger&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:10.500 --> 03:41:15.899
details of events that followed this test have&nbsp;
been redacted from the official file but a note&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:15.899 --> 03:41:21.839
from a member of the OverWatch Council provides&nbsp;
a peek into what might have happened scp-2241&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:21.840 --> 03:41:26.939
has stated that it intends to grow stronger to&nbsp;
stop more people from dying and this will help&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:26.939 --> 03:41:33.000
both it and Us in this aim killing a man with a&nbsp;
teleported bullet was a stroke of tactical genius&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:33.000 --> 03:41:39.660
from the SCP object MTF Theta 17 will be ready to&nbsp;
respond during all further rounds of testing as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:39.660 --> 03:41:45.359
precaution following a series of tests Each of&nbsp;
which included heightened emotional Stakes such&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:45.359 --> 03:41:51.660
as threatening the lives of innocent bystanders&nbsp;
or treasured items belonging to scp-2241 his&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:51.660 --> 03:41:57.540
abilities developed even further in one test a&nbsp;
series of armed drones were made to artificially&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:41:57.540 --> 03:42:03.120
malfunction posing an apparent threat to&nbsp;
Foundation Personnel around the boy he responded&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:03.120 --> 03:42:08.700
by using his telekinesis to turn the drones on&nbsp;
each other crashing them into one another while&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:08.700 --> 03:42:15.059
only one drone remained he teleported its Weaponry&nbsp;
to a nearby Field leaving a harmless shell behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:15.060 --> 03:42:20.580
in another test a bomb was detonated near a&nbsp;
member of d-class personnel the boy somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:20.580 --> 03:42:26.760
absorbed the energy of the bomb as it exploded&nbsp;
transforming its kinetic energy and saving the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:26.760 --> 03:42:32.580
man's life another bomb related test featured man&nbsp;
with a bomb strapped to him attacking a d-class&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:42:32.580 --> 03:42:38.160
in this test it was ordered that the bomber be&nbsp;
